<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cataract-surgery">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cataract surgery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cataract surgery is the treatment of the clouding of the eye's lens. In ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the surgical compendium attributed to the physician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sushruta">Sushruta</a> described a technique of couching the cataract. The site cites this, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhinoplasty">rhinoplasty</a>, among the medical achievements associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>'s scientific culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cataract-surgery.jpg" alt="Cataract surgery" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto Haab and George E. de Schweinitz · No restrictions · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_and_epitome_of_operative_ophthalmology_(1905)_(14782610945).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
